Assessment Rules
•	Base all classifications solely on the information contained in the source data.
•	Do not infer or assume control activities, risk coverage, process steps, dependencies, ownership, effectiveness, or relationships that are not explicitly described.
•	Do not create fragmented, redundant, or common control relationships without sufficient supporting evidence.
•	Where the available information is insufficient to confidently determine a relationship between controls, classify the outcome as Unclear and explain why.
•	Do not assume that controls are redundant solely because they contain similar wording.
•	Do not assume that controls are fragmented solely because they belong to the same Control Objective Group.
•	Do not assume that controls are common controls solely because they operate within the same product, process, or payment stage.
•	Look for evidence of overlapping control objectives, activities, inputs, outputs, or risk outcomes before assigning a rationalisation classification.
•	Apply classifications consistently across all controls within the assessment scope.

Confidence Assessment
•	Assign a confidence rating for every assessment outcome:
•	High: Strong evidence supports the classification.
•	Medium: Some evidence supports the classification, but minor assumptions or interpretation were required.
•	Low: Limited evidence is available and the classification should be treated as indicative only.
•	Unclear Classification

Assign Unclear where:
•	The control description lacks sufficient detail.
•	The relationship between controls cannot be determined from the available information.
•	There is insufficient evidence to conclude that a control is redundant, fragmented, or a common control opportunity.
•	Multiple interpretations are reasonably possible.

Critical Output Rule
•	Do not force a rationalisation outcome. A control should only be classified as Redundant, Process-Split Fragmentation, or Common Control Opportunity where sufficient evidence exists. If sufficient evidence does not exist, classify the control as Unclear and provide the reason.
